# Research Engine — Autonomous Research Workflow Engine

A LangGraph-powered research engine that plans its own research strategy,
executes three research threads in genuine parallel (each its own compiled
subgraph), synthesizes the findings, checks itself for completeness, and
loops back to fill in gaps before publishing a final report.

---

## What It Does

Give it a research topic, and the engine will:

- **Plan** — Break the topic into 3 distinct research angles (or, on a repeat
  pass, into 3 targeted queries addressing previously found gaps)
- **Research in Parallel** — Run all 3 angles concurrently, each through its own
  compiled subgraph (`search → summarize`), using real Tavily web search and
  real Groq summarization
- **Synthesize** — Combine all findings so far into one coherent draft
- **Check for Gaps** — Ask an LLM judge whether the synthesis is comprehensive
- **Loop if Needed** — If gaps are found (and the iteration cap hasn't been hit),
  plan additional targeted research and repeat
- **Publish** — Once complete, generate a polished final report

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Orchestration | LangGraph `StateGraph` |
| Parallel Execution | `concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor` running 3 compiled subgraphs |
| Web Search | Tavily (real, live results) |
| LLM | Groq (`llama-3.1-8b-instant`) — planning, summarizing, synthesizing, judging, writing |
| Language | Python 3.11+ |

